# A trailing slash matches a directory only, so a *symlink* of the same name slips past the
# rule and gets committed. That happened twice in one afternoon — `node_modules` and
# `contracts/lib`, both symlinks made in a worktree to skip a reinstall, both carrying an
# absolute home path into a public repository. No trailing slashes here.

